So what?

Most players in most games never _see_ the midgame,
and high charisma is a very important part of
success in the early game.

You're patching in terms of how the game is seen
from the viewpoint of the most highly skilled
players, ignoring the vast bulk of the NetHack
audience, a definite no-no.

Credit cloning is _much_ more successful with a
charisma of 17 than with a charisma of 7; it goes
many times as quickly, and so the PC's chances of
being killed while attempting it drop dramatically;
the high charisma of healer's is one of the few
things they have going for them in the early game.

Purchasing goods is much easier with high charisma.

The difference for an early-game player might be
only an extra couple of daggers to quiver, but that
can be all the edge needed to survive the early
game, and gives a chance to enhance dagger skills
toward the machine-gunning level earlier and thus
more meaningfully. Many other purchasable items in
NetHack can have equally dramatic odds-improving
effects if gained early in the game, and high
charisma makes all the difference if the items are
to be _bought_,

By removing charisma, you are removing a tool that a
player can use as an edge to survive <em>to the
point</em> where it become irrelevant.

I think you are way underestimating the value of
charisma to the game.

This patch is purely a mistake, best I can tell.

